WEBVTT

00:00.300 --> 00:04.990
New Mercury? The first few hours
shape how it runs for years.

00:05.580 --> 00:07.030
Here's how to break it in right.

00:08.736 --> 00:11.536
Start with the owner's
manual for your exact motor.

00:11.556 --> 00:15.426
Break-in rules differ
between Mercury models.

00:16.136 --> 00:23.426
Mercury's own 150 Pro XS example runs 10
hours, but your book has the final say.

00:24.695 --> 00:27.865
New piston rings are still seating
against the cylinder walls.

00:28.575 --> 00:31.505
Changing RPM helps them seat evenly.

00:32.575 --> 00:38.045
Hold one speed for hours and the walls
can glaze, so the rings never seal right.

00:39.296 --> 00:42.666
Warm it up and check for
a steady tell-tale stream.

00:43.516 --> 00:45.006
Then keep the throttle moving.

00:45.556 --> 00:51.326
Avoid long runs at one speed, keep wide-open
throttle within your manual's limits,

00:51.746 --> 00:54.206
and go easy on heavy loads.

00:55.647 --> 00:57.737
Break-in isn't your first service.

00:58.467 --> 01:00.767
For most current FourStrokes,

01:00.787 --> 01:06.137
Mercury's first scheduled service
is at 100 hours or once a year.

01:06.787 --> 01:11.677
Our optional early oil change around
20 hours is dealer best practice,

01:12.207 --> 01:13.937
not a warranty requirement.

01:15.368 --> 01:20.458
Mercury says damage from improper
break-in may not be covered by warranty.

01:21.208 --> 01:25.298
The full guide is at mercuryrepower.ca.
